# Snooping Page: "can't be blocked this turn" only restricts blockers not yet declared (CR 509.1b-c). Ornithopter blocks it first;
# then Bot1 casts Silverquill Charm on it in the declare blockers step, and the Repartee trigger resolves. Page stays blocked
# (CR 509.1h), deals its damage to Ornithopter and none to Bot2, so its damage trigger doesn't fire and Bot1 neither draws nor loses life.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Pearl
Mox Jet
Plains
Snooping Page
Silverquill Charm
Plains x2
Plains x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter
Mountain x19

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Snooping Page.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Snooping Page > Bot2)
Bot2.Block(Ornithopter > Snooping Page)
[T3 Bot1.DeclareBlockers]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Silverquill Charm.Cast
Bot1.Modes(1)
Bot1.Target(Bot1.Battlefield.Snooping Page)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 20
Bot1.Life = 20
Bot2.Graveyard = Ornithopter
